    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    Startup - From Launch to Lobby.

    v1.0.18 • Production Release — Browser Events, Minimap HUD, Essentials & Attribution Safety
    • Added Startup Browser live join/event notifications with sliding cards, Developer-hosted Event popups, owner-only End Event controls, and a full five-second on-screen hold.
    • Added the expanded-minimap HUD adapter with reliable Z detection, player-count pre-scan, smooth frame-based animation, static Advertise HUD placement, and automatic 10-second restore.
    • Trigger Bot now persists its enabled state and reaction delay, with a 20 ms default reaction delay. Region HUD remains ON by default unless the user explicitly disables it.
    • Added the Essentials Death Log with saved default-ON state and contextual death-cause messages, then simplified its UI to a clean toggle directly below Trigger Bot.
    • Events now publish and display GTA V Version: Legacy or Enhanced in red across the Events tab, Live Event cards, notifications, and popups while remaining visible cross-edition. Wrong-edition Event JOIN attempts are stopped after the Before You Join acknowledgement with a dedicated compatibility notice.
    • Added proximity/same-vehicle explosion attribution safety. Standalone explosion flags are quarantined when attribution is unsafe, including passengers/nearby players and local Explosive Ammo proximity, while independent strong evidence remains active.
    • Build 479 adds a configurable Auto-Bounty Killer delay (Instant, 10s, 30s, 1m, 3m, 5m, 10m), defaults to 1 minute, persists the selection, and revalidates delayed targets before applying the built-in 9k bounty.
    • Build 480 keeps Kill Retaliation enabled by default but makes Auto-Bounty Killer opt-in by default, while persisting the retaliation controls across restarts.
    • Build 481 fixes Auto-Bounty Killer OFF persistence across Startup reloads by reinstalling the retaliation config wrapper on every script load and explicitly saving/restoring the OFF boolean.
    • Build 434 is the v1.0.18 production promotion of the user-approved B433 branch.
    • Build 435 production hotfix: Host HUD OFF now suppresses every Session Host line, Event View Now opens the current EVENTS hub correctly, and current Startup branding is normalized to v1.0.18.
    • Build 436 production hotfix: verified Event attendees are prompted for feedback when the host ends the Event, changes sessions, or goes offline; LIVE attendance refresh is accelerated.
    • Build 437 adds a vehicle-only MPH / KMH HUD directly below Connected Players and automatically suppresses it while DriftGod is running.
    • Build 438 removes redundant internal pcall layers while preserving Cherax/native/file/network/render safety boundaries.
    • Build 439 classifies PTFX and Stun Gun detections as non-modder noise and repairs stale noise-only modder records.
    • Build 441 is the production-clean release: late hotfix metadata is consolidated, redundant internal guards are reduced further, and current v1.0.18 release identity is normalized.

    Previous Production Release — Prime Hosting, Any Advertise & HUD Polish
    • Added Prime: Host Public Sessions in Config. It defaults ON, persists, and keeps Prime on New Public Session for normal hosting and diagnostic return-to-host behavior until the user turns it OFF.
    • Added Any Advertise: Matchmaking Override Region = Any, Advertise Region = My Region, and Advertise Session = ON, with capability-validated exact-label resolution, no automatic rotation, and session-change reapply.
    • Moved Show Region Type in HUD to the HUD tab only, added a red players-not-joining Guide reminder, and reduced the Simulate First-Time Setup Config-label font size.
    • Fixed the Build 410 main-chunk 200-local-variable failure by namespacing two late helpers without removing Any Advertise or other production functionality.
    • Removed Prime's unconditional automatic return to Join Public Session while Prime hosting is enabled; turning the Config toggle OFF restores Join Public Session behavior.
    • Removed the duplicate Region Type HUD control from the advertising/flow UI so HUD display controls now live in the HUD tab.
    • Build 413 hotfix: Any Advertise now validates that the targeted Matchmaking control actually exposes the exact Any option before writing, fixing the safe Override Region write failure seen on some Cherax layouts.
    • Build 414 hotfix: selecting an Advertising Method now starts applying it immediately, and Any Advertise supports Cherax layouts where Override Region is visible in ClickGUI but its list is hidden from Lua; the exact Override Region control uses the user-confirmed My Region=0 / Any=1 layout with index/current-string verification.
    • Build 415 polish: selecting any Advertising Method also turns Auto Advertise Session ON; Activity Background Alpha now defaults to 60; Activity Feed X defaults to 0.174 while automatic HUD-stack Y anchoring stays active.
    • Build 416 production release: promotes the user-confirmed B415 behavior unchanged, with final previous-production metadata, changelog acknowledgement, and release packaging.
    • Build 417 production hotfix: when GTA Online becomes ready, Startup immediately turns Auto Advertise Session ON, starts the saved production advertising method, and attempts Advertise Session ON at once while keeping region writes serialized/host-safe; Guide content is refreshed for the current production workflow.
    • Build 418 production hotfix: Activity Feed X is now read live from its slider at render time and the final runtime position resolver uses that X value even with Auto Position enabled; 0.174 remains the production default.

    v1.0.16 • Advertising, HUD & Reliability
    • Updated Startup for the current Cherax Advertise Session / Advertise Region layout and improved theme, HUD, and session-routing reliability.
    • Added Cherax ID primary account linking, true global Startup Users Online presence, and additional BattlEye timeout / self-kick safety guards.
    • Expanded advertising research and production methods, culminating in Standard Advertise, Region Advertise, and Synced Region Advertise with serialized ownership and stable-session checks.
    • Refined the Session Activity/HUD layout, sizing, placement, and production-safe renderer behavior while hiding internal advertising-method test UI from the published build.

    v1.0.15 • Join Fixes & Prime Browser Preparation
    • Fixed Startup Browser JOIN issues, including verified Startup RID / Saved Players compatibility that could incorrectly stop authenticated joins.
    • Improved JOIN transition reliability while preserving Community Trust protections for verified Startup users.
    • Disenrolled users now get a closed Browser tab message instead of Browser popup/UI content; Privacy Alias, Disenroll, and new Blacklist JOIN blocking default OFF.
    • Started preparing Startup Browser for the upcoming Prime version while keeping the current Browser release stable.
    • Auto Start renderer-safety hotfix: hidden RID Session discovery stays dormant; Browser, PlayerTracker, and asset workers remain staggered; early render/event callbacks no longer perform diagnostic/support file I/O.
    • Browser JOIN single-flight safety: session starts cancel pending JOINs cleanly, duplicate JOIN clicks are absorbed, stale JOINs expire faster, and unrelated-session landings abort instead of lingering.
    • Production promotion: B360 JOIN/Auto Start safety is retained; final timeout tuning gives slow EE RID joins up to 90 seconds to settle before cleanup.

    v1.0.13 • Startup Browser
    • Launched Startup Browser live sessions and Events with authenticated JOIN, profiles, Favorites, and Community Reputation.
    • Added Browser moderation, personal blocks, verified-user safeguards, and host/session safety controls.
    • Added automatic Browser asset delivery, recovery/fallback behavior, and production-ready UI polish.
    • Improved session advertising, JOIN guidance, and real same-session PING.

    v1.0.11 • Session, HUD & Defense
    • Added time-aware Enhanced advertising modes and improved session routing.
    • Expanded Startup HUD/activity cards, NAT/region recovery, and Prime support.
    • Strengthened crash/kick handling, RID history, and modder classification safety.
    • Added Startup Browser/backend foundations, ticketed RID JOIN, and moderation tools.
    • Improved onboarding, diagnostics, support ZIPs, OneDrive support, and stability.

    v1.0.10 • Production Stability
    • Fixed blank-menu/theme/session startup issues and Enhanced advertising support.
    • Improved NAT, settings discovery, Prime routing, diagnostics, and guided setup.

    Developed by: Public_Urinal
    Credits: Built with assistance from ChatGPT.
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
]]
local STARTUP_DUPLICATE_GUARD_HASH = 0x17E3FFB8

local function startup_duplicate_guard_log(message)
    if Logger and Logger.LogInfo then
        Logger.LogInfo("[Startup] " .. tostring(message))
    elseif print then
        print("[Startup] " .. tostring(message))
    end
end

if FeatureMgr and FeatureMgr.GetFeature then
    local existingStartupFeature = FeatureMgr.GetFeature(STARTUP_DUPLICATE_GUARD_HASH)
    if existingStartupFeature ~= nil then
        startup_duplicate_guard_log("Duplicate copy blocked. Startup is already running. Unload either the subscribed Startup script or the local Startup.lua copy.")
        return
    end
end

